# XSH creal(), crealf() and creall()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Only what the page makes exact is tested: values returned unchanged or with
# a stated sign change, including signed zeros, infinities and NaN parts.
# Arguments are built with CMPLX() and pass through volatile objects, and the
# three types (name, name with f, name with l) are each tested. Infinite and
# NaN cases are skipped where the type has none.

assertion  XSH.creal.001
anchor     functions/creal.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/creal.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       creal returns the real part of a finite value exactly: 1.5 + 2.5i
           gives 1.5, -3 + 4i gives -3, 0.25 - 0.5i gives 0.25.
test       t/001-finite.c

assertion  XSH.creal.002
anchor     functions/creal.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/creal.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       creal returns a zero real part with its sign (for a type with
           negative zero), whatever the imaginary part is.
test       t/002-signed-zero.c

assertion  XSH.creal.003
anchor     functions/creal.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/creal.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       creal returns an infinite or NaN real part as it is, and the real
           part when the imaginary part is infinite or NaN.
test       t/003-infinite-nan.c
